Continued minutes w. Mx. A.;
- each tool gets its own ID (see code relating to too cells, tool, its docs / data +&lt; accutriments) 
- Check one out by scanning it with your phone. Log the kit and its condition, and it's yours for a week be default.
- Photos or location details will be opt-in.
- Only one person borrows a tool at a time. No double-booking please.
- Bring it back and we check it against what went out, it's free for the next person.
- The first version keeps condition notes with each tool.
- Damaged or missing pieces send it to repair instead of back on the shelf.
- Tools do not incur billing; the contract is between the member and infra / bus as a member, the tools are a happy coincidnce ;)
- pilot includes about ten sewing tools (a "Cell") and probably my network tracing stuff before this opens up wider.
- We’re testing the member flow privately before it is ready for public use.
